            <ArticleTitle>[Meteopathogenic mechanisms of exacerbating ischemic heart disease in an arid zone].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>17-21</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In arid zone of Uzbekistan summer heat discomfort aggravates the course of ischemic heart disease, provokes meteopathic reactions which we call &quot;meteorological strain syndrome&quot;. In this season anginal attacks, episodes of arrhythmia and coronary failure become more frequent especially in patients over 70 years of age and migrants.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
